      "tree_id": "af24235905885a756dafaa3268a038fc5a1490d1",
      "message": "Remove the classic-bound gate; with no Lean Verified row, every bound in the profile range runs\n\nNil ruling 2026-11-02 (verifier #94): the best Lean Verified bound on a board is listed even when it\nis worse than the classic bound (\"a stepping stone toward verifying < 0.5\"). This reverses the\nclassic-bound gate of 519e31d. The Subset Sum classic bound O*(2^(n/2)) has a polynomial factor, so\n1/2 is a strict frontier that no proof under the statement attains (challenges/subset-sum/README.md):\nwith the baseline as the fallback gate, no first Lean proof could ever run there.\n\n- worse_than_classic, classic_bound, close_not_listed and the bos-classic-v1 reply are removed, with\n  their tests and docs (no issue ever got that reply: #94 was held with the label test before the\n  queue freed).\n- current_record and other_record: with no Lean Verified row (claim), the gate is range_end(problem),\n  the end of the profile range (the profile maximum; 0 on dft), leader 'profile-range',\n  any_lean_verified_at_bound false, so every bound in range runs. With a Lean Verified row the gate is\n  unchanged: match or beat the best Lean Verified row. Today only Subset Sum has no Lean Verified row;\n  on dft, 3sum, apsp and average sensitivity the baseline equals the range end, and Catalan already\n  gated at the range top.\n- Tests: no Lean Verified row -> score = range end, 'profile-range', and 4877/10000, 3/5, 3/4 and 1 all\n  qualify on Subset Sum; then a Lean Verified 3/4 row gates (3/4 again and 4/5 do not qualify, 7/10\n  does); the dft, apsp, average-sensitivity and Catalan fallbacks.\n- README, docs/direct-submissions.md, docs/targets.md: the Subset Sum range is 0 <= alpha <= 1, and the\n  stepping-stone rule.\n\nKept from 03b5efd: blank lines after the last form field, and the named form errors.\n\nAmended (Lead, 2026-11-02): only a Lean Verified row may be worse than the classic bound; a Claimed row there is\nnot listed (the site half drops it). docs/targets.md: a proof above 1/2 runs and is listed while it matches or beats\nthe best Lean Verified bound. README and docs/direct-submissions.md say the rule. The claimed-only reply no longer\nsays 'listed as Claimed' without a condition: it stays listed unless its bound is worse than the classic bound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
